    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #287\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed successfully to branch `bb/relay-105-inbox-pipeline-06-07-confirm-reject-an-thr_c2g93czrgc`.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplements issue #105: confirm, reject, and revise for Processing proposals.\n\n- **`inbox/proposalActions.ts`** (new): `confirmProposalWithClient`, `rejectProposalWithClient`, `reviseProposalWithClient`.\n  - Confirm is the sole cross-destination write path: `database` envelopes go through the existing `createItemWithClient` choke point; `pageContent` envelopes go through a new `putBlockWithClient`. Persists `resultItemId`/`resultLabel` and locks `confirmed`. Idempotent under retry.\n  - Reject locks `rejected` with no destination write; idempotent; refuses an already-confirmed proposal.\n  - Revise replaces the complete envelope (including `entityKind`, so it can switch atomically between `database` and `pageContent`), appends a user-authored history entry, and refuses a locked proposal.\n- **`docs/docPersistence.ts` / `docs/docStore.ts`**: added client-scoped `mutateDocWithClient`/`putBlockWithClient` so a page-content block append commits in the same transaction as the proposal's `confirmed` lock.\n- **`inbox/inboxTickAction.ts`**: exported `appendHistoryEntry` (now with a selectable author) and `assertValidProposalEnvelope` for reuse.\n- **`manifest/permissionManifest.ts`**: added `writable` to `ManifestDatabase` and scoped Semprec's own project grant so Inbox/Inbox item types are read-only and only Processing proposals is writable (grant separation).\n- New tests in `proposalActions.test.ts` and a grant-separation test in `manifest.test.ts`.\n\nFull workspace build and test suite (307 tests) pass.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
