    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #287\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed to the existing branch `bb/relay-105-inbox-pipeline-06-07-confirm-reject-an-thr_c2g93czrgc` (updates PR #287), fast-forward `ff29e22..596e51b`.\n\n## Summary\n\nAddressed the two blocking findings from the code-review CI run on PR #287:\n\n- **High (notification-before-commit):** `appendDocUpdateWithClient` was firing the realtime `notifyDocUpdate` hook immediately after inserting the `doc_updates` row, while the surrounding transaction (e.g. `confirmProposalWithClient`, which also updates the proposal's status) was still open — a later rollback could leave subscribers having observed a write that never persisted. Added a generic `runAfterCommit(client, callback)` primitive to `db/pool.ts`'s `withTransaction` and deferred the notification through it.\n- **Medium (missing input validation):** `assertValidProposalEnvelope`'s `database` branch only checked that the target existed, not whether it was one of Semprec's own read-only-to-the-agent databases (Inbox, Inbox item types) — so a user-supplied `revise` could retarget a proposal there and bypass the manifest's `writable: false`. Extracted the shared module-id list to `seed/inboxPipelineKeys.ts`'s `SEMPREC_READ_ONLY_MODULE_IDS` (now reused by both the manifest and this validation) and reject such targets.\n\nAdded regression tests for both. Full build and test suite verified green (310/310 tests) before pushing.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
